        <type></type>
        <name>Metric</name>
        <qualifiedname>hmap::TerrainTriMesh::MeshPathCostConfig::Metric</qualifiedname>
        <enumvalue id="structhmap_1_1TerrainTriMesh_1_1MeshPathCostConfig_1a273ae8b085bc1309827cb47afdc2ea9aaa0127f42b58ed1e4feff9b17a290ded7" prot="public">
          <name>EUCLIDEAN_2D</name>
          <briefdescription>
<para>Pure 2D Euclidean distance in the XY plane. </para>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="structhmap_1_1TerrainTriMesh_1_1Edge" kindref="compound">Edge</ref> cost is simply the 2D segment length: <formula id="36">$ \text{cost} = d_{2D} $</formula> </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="structhmap_1_1TerrainTriMesh_1_1MeshPathCostConfig_1a273ae8b085bc1309827cb47afdc2ea9aa3db07082ff51d740670b0f24f3a1cb79" prot="public">
          <name>SYMMETRIC_Z</name>
          <briefdescription>
<para>Symmetric elevation change metric. </para>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Treats uphill and downhill elevation changes equally: <formula id="37">$ \text{cost} = |\Delta z| + w_{elev} \cdot z_{curr} $</formula> where <formula id="38">$ w_{elev} $</formula> is <ref refid="structhmap_1_1TerrainTriMesh_1_1MeshPathCostConfig_1aa4e659b73d4ea2a70567d9659f1475ee" kindref="member">elevation_weight</ref>. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="structhmap_1_1TerrainTriMesh_1_1MeshPathCostConfig_1a273ae8b085bc1309827cb47afdc2ea9aab372763954316f3e914ee39ce92124ef" prot="public">
          <name>HYDROLOGICAL</name>
          <briefdescription>
<para>Asymmetric hydrological flow metric for streams. </para>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Strongly penalizes uphill steps while favoring natural downhill flow:      <formula id="39">\[  \text{cost} = (1 - r_{elev}) \cdot d_{2D}
              + (\Delta z &gt; 0 \;?\; p_{up} \cdot (\Delta
z)^{e_{dist}} : |\Delta z|)
              + r_{elev} \cdot \max(0, \Delta z)
\]</formula> where <formula id="40">$ r_{elev} $</formula> is <ref refid="structhmap_1_1TerrainTriMesh_1_1MeshPathCostConfig_1a9c91dda4b33f7152939aafa0ca77ab4d" kindref="member">elevation_ratio</ref>,  <formula id="41">$e_{dist} $</formula> is <ref refid="structhmap_1_1TerrainTriMesh_1_1MeshPathCostConfig_1a51a7a21b3029516eb39be45b2d8b15f1" kindref="member">distance_exponent</ref>, and <formula id="42">$ p_{up} $</formula> is <ref refid="structhmap_1_1TerrainTriMesh_1_1MeshPathCostConfig_1a1232bf5b364db44d55bf012e29066c3d" kindref="member">upward_penalization</ref>. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Cost metric model used for edge traversal. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
        </detaileddescription>
